  "decision": "Closed",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed gates, by reason of their contemporary design, would represent an incongruous form of development that would erode the original appearance of the host property and would introduce a discordant feature within the streetscape. The scheme would cause less than substantial harm to the Sheen Common Drive Conservation Area of which it forms part, and there are no public benefits to outweigh this harm. As such, the proposal would be contrary to the NPPF (2024), the Richmond Local Plan (2025), in particular policies LP28 and LP29, the House Extensions and External Alterations (2015) Supplementary Planning Document, as supported by the CA69 Sheen Common Drive Conservation Area Statement."
